    "function": "contrast",
    "source_turn_preview_server_only": "During another stage, called REM sleep, the eyes move rapidly while the sleeper remains largely still. Researchers have explored links with emotional processing and skill learning. However, people do not need to memorise stage names to benefit from adequate rest. A practical principle is to maintain a regular schedule, so the body has a predictable opportunity to sleep."
